   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "An alternative to this split-up would be to keep having only one \"full\" (i.e. non-static) context and use it for both signing and verifying",
   "request": "Keep only one non-static context for both signing and verifying instead of splitting them",
   "status": "accepted",
   "status_by": {
    "at": "2026-09-30",
    "by": "theStack",
    "id": "rc:4146895271",
    "quote": "Fair point, I didn't consider that there could be potential use-cases where the context needs any further modification a"
   },
   "status_note": "theStack accepted furszy's explanation that separate contexts avoid adding a mutex on verification for thread safety if re-seeding is ever needed",
   "type": "suggestion",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36188#discussion_r4145797706"
  },
  {
   "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
